<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-dim7-to-dom7" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>dim7 to Dom7</title>

  <p>
    Because a diminished seventh chord consists entirely of stacked minor thirds, every
    one of its four notes sits exactly one semitone above a note that belongs to a dominant
    seventh chord. Lowering any one note of a Ddim7 chord (D–F–A<flat />–B) by one semitone
    therefore produces a dominant 7th chord: lower B → B<flat />7; lower A<flat /> → G7;
    lower F → E7; lower D → D<flat />7. All four results are shown below.
  </p>

  <figure xml:id="fig-chord-grids-p3-row3">
    <caption>Ddim7 (D–F–A<flat />–B) as source chord, and the four dominant 7th chords
    produced by lowering each note by one semitone in turn. Row 1: the Ddim7 shape.
    Row 2 (left to right): B<flat />7 (lower B → B<flat />); G7 (lower A<flat /> → G);
    E7 (lower F → E); D<flat />7 (lower D → D<flat />).</caption>
    <sbsgroup>

      <!-- ===== Row 1: Ddim7 source grid (centred) ===== -->
      <sidebyside widths="22%" margins="39%">
        <image xml:id="img-grid-p3-ddim7">
          <latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.65, transform shape]
\pgfmathsetmacro{\isoangle}{60}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vv}{8}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hh}{6}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\vlen}{0.85}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ang}{\isoangle/2}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\dlen}{(\vlen/2) / sin(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\hlen}{(\vlen/2) / tan(\ang)}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\xmax}{\hh*\hlen}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\ymax}{\vv*\vlen}
\drawgridandnotes
\gn{5}{1.5}{C}{0}
\gn{4}{2}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{3}{2.5}{D}{1}
\gn{2}{3}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{3.5}{E}{0}
\gn{5}{2.5}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{3}{E}{0}
\gn{3}{3.5}{F}{1}
\gn{2}{4}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{4.5}{G}{0}
\gn{5}{3.5}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{4}{G}{0}
\gn{3}{4.5}{A$\flat$, G$\sharp$}{1}
\gn{2}{5}{A}{0}
\gn{1}{5.5}{B$\flat$, A$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{5}{4.5}{A}{0}
\gn{4}{5}{B$\flat$, A$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{3}{5.5}{B}{1}
\gn{2}{6}{C}{0}
\gn{1}{6.5}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{5}{5.5}{C}{0}
\gn{4}{6}{C$\sharp$, D$\flat$}{0}
\gn{3}{6.5}{D}{0}
\gn{2}{7}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{7.5}{E}{0}
\gn{5}{6.5}{E$\flat$, D$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{4}{7}{E}{0}
\gn{3}{7.5}{F}{0}
\gn{2}{8}{G$\flat$, F$\sharp$}{0}
\gn{1}{8.5}{G}{0}
\draw[black!40, semithick, rounded corners=6pt] ({2*\hlen- 0.60},{2.5*\vlen- 0.60}) rectangle ({3*\hlen+ 0.60},{5.5*\vlen+ 0.60});
\end{tikzpicture}
          </latex-image>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>

      <!-- Notation for Ddim7 (centred) -->
      <sidebyside widths="8%" margins="46%">
        <image xml:id="img-notation-p3-ddim7" source="notation/chord-ddim7">
          <shortdescription>Ddim7 chord on treble staff</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </sidebyside>

